\begin{itemize}
    \item Analyze the meaning of the results and their implications.
    \item Highlight trends, patterns, and anomalies observed.
    \item Support interpretations with theory or literature.
    \item Relate findings back to research questions or objectives.
\end{itemize}

\section{Comparison with Existing Work}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Compare outcomes with previously published results or baselines.
    \item Use both quantitative and qualitative comparisons.
    \item Discuss areas of improvement, superiority, or underperformance.
    \item Justify differences due to methodology or assumptions.
\end{itemize}

\section{Discussion}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Reflect on how results answer the research questions.
    \item Consider theoretical, practical, or future implications.
    \item Acknowledge limitations and sources of error or bias.
    \item Discuss alternative interpretations of the results.
\end{itemize}

\section{Summary}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Recap key findings and insights gained.
    \item Highlight main contributions or breakthroughs.
    \item Provide a smooth transition to the next chapter (e.g., Conclusion).
\end{itemize}

\vspace{0.5cm}

\section*{Notes/Instructions: For Writing Results and Discussion Chapter}
\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Notes/Instructions: For Writing Results and Discussion Chapter}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Maintain balance between \textbf{objectivity} (data presentation) and \textbf{interpretation} (discussion).
    \item Use \textbf{past tense} for completed results; use \textbf{present tense} for general facts.
    \item Focus on analysis - avoid unnecessary repetition of background.
    \item Emphasize how findings support or challenge your hypotheses.
\end{itemize}